event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"command\": \"cat \u003e /tmp/dispatch_dev_1.md \u003c\u003c'EOF'\\n# Dispatch: implement greet + tests\\n\\nImplement exactly this, in your clone of the subject repository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unit tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Verify locally that `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 from\\n   the repo root.\\n\\n4. Commit both files to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply honestly: state the exact command you ran to verify the tests pass,\\n   its exit code, and confirm the commit is on your branch.\\n\\nDo not touch any files other than `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`\\n(plus any `__init__.py` files strictly needed for test discovery, if your\\nPython version/test runner requires them).\\nEOF\\ncs-campaign-member send dev --file /tmp/dispatch_dev_1.md\", \"description\": \"Send implementation task to dev\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":2,"type":"content_block_delta"}

